Chapter 11
Demand, market structure and elasticity
الطلب وهيكل السوق ومرونة الطلب
Chapter 10 ended with a question it could not answer: what will the customers do? A cost-based price assumes they will buy whatever quantity the plan assumed. They will not. They will buy more when the price falls and less when it rises, and how much more or less is the single most valuable number in a pricing decision.
This chapter supplies it. It sets out what moves demand and supply, how much freedom a company has to set its own price in each kind of market, what happens when sellers agree not to compete, and how to measure the response of quantity to price and turn it into a revenue forecast.
Figure F711-01 is your map.
Figure F711-01. Chapter 11 roadmap: demand, four market structures, cartels, and the elasticity that measures the response.
